<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Stefanos Vogoridis</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1775–1859</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Stefan Bogoridi</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Stefanos Vogoridis was a Bulgarian-born Ottoman statesman of the Phanariot circle. In 1834 the Porte appointed him the first prince of the autonomous Principality of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samo">Samos</a>, which he governed through deputies from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantinople">Constantinople</a> until 1850. He also served as caimacam of Moldavia in 1821–1822.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/stefanos-vogoridis.jpg" alt="Stefanos Vogoridis" width="320" height="471" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Stefan_Bogoridi2.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
